What does the following recursive function return for fun(5)?
```c
int fun(int n) {
  if (n <= 1) return 1;
  if (n % 2 == 0) return fun(n / 2);
  return fun(n - 1) + fun(n - 2);
}
```

What is the output of the following C program?
```c
#include <stdio.h>
int main() {
  int arr[] = {10, 20, 30, 40, 50};
  int *ptr = arr;
  printf("%d ", *(ptr + 2));
  printf("%d", *ptr++);
  return 0;
}
```

